      "writtenOn": "2014-10-12T16:41:59Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I\u0027d like to determine supplier + charge port based on data that I know not to be changing. With the current code, I cannot find any fatal bugs that can happen as a result of data changing mid-calculation. But, it would be easy to write such code -- for example, determine supplier by checking for non-zero current, then make another complete pass through the table with the wrong assumption that we have non-zero charge current for that supplier.\n\nLet\u0027s get another opinion about it.",
